From 01eeb65c8a9a24ee722f693bab9eef66b917373f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:46:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] :new: Let a VM's settings turn video acceleration off

A user asked to be able to turn off the VideoToolbox and M2 scaler devices
that 054ac2080 gave every VM on reims-vgpu, the host's hardware video decode,
encode and scaling for the guest.

A VM's settings gain video_acceleration, on unless they say off, so every
existing vm.toml loads and saves as before. Off, the VM has neither device,
on x86-64 and arm64 alike, and the guest decodes, encodes and scales video in
software; the command line is then the one every VM ran before 054ac2080. On,
it is unchanged. The edit form has a Video acceleration toggle, hidden on
VMware SVGA, which has neither device either way; `set` takes
--video-acceleration[=false], and `show` gives its state. The OpenCore image
is unchanged: with the devices off, its video kexts match nothing.

(cherry picked from commit f6b7e92720b886707b3a97f2c695dd066868adae)
